Hy4-flash oracle prompts: the text of each prompt and its token ids, one decimal id a line, no chat template and no BOS (the
file's tokenizer adds none: llama-tokenize gives the same ids with and without --no-bos, which `hy4-oracle.sh --prompts` checks
before it writes a file). A dump of this model's logits takes its ids from here and never tokenizes (tools/ref/cb_dump.cpp): a
tokenizer difference would read as a kernel bug.

Made once, on the box, by the tokenizer of the dump's own tree (llama.cpp PR #32517, "Model : add hy_v4_flash support", head
0a054d0b02454c998e068381d15f3f6615bdd987, version 1.0.0-dev (build 12473, commit 0a054d0b0), CPU build, no patch) on shard 1 of
Tencent's Hy4-flash-Q4_K_M GGUF (the vocabulary is in shard 1; the pre-tokenizer is `hy_v4`), by
`MODEL=<shard 1> bash crates/tokenizer/tools/hy4-oracle.sh --prompts tools/ref/data/hy4`:

    llama-tokenize -m <shard 1> -f <text> --ids --no-escape --log-disable     # "[id, id, ...]", written one id a line

The texts hold no final newline (one would be an id) and no backslash. They are the four prompts of exaone-moe's set
(tools/ref/data/exaone-moe, the same bytes and sha256), so every model's dump runs the same texts. Our tokenizer gives the same ids
for all four: crates/tokenizer/tests/hy4.rs holds them (`hw_hy4_oracle_prompts_encode_to_their_pinned_ids`), beside the 112 cases of
`hy4-ids.tsv`.

    a  32 ids  English paragraph, cut after "coming home."   txt 139 bytes
       ids b16c4628b32aa12e4b66350e3b3b26ffa7a40f96481e22c4e2f34fac1e01a083
       text bcb98a9e563eabdcbd4a4c4cbb3e7b8de220e51006ba45c7bdbac07acc36149c
    b  31 ids  Korean paragraph, cut after "단풍이"             txt 97 bytes
       ids eff9cd2dd8a580a4c158fc971c8caae0e581c8f89bf5c13141cb5102f23f0bac
       text 63ed34c308dcab881c36fef27c3d51bfc8d516ab3bd687424a33c44a0d159e22
    c  30 ids  Rust function head, cut after `HashMap::new();` txt 115 bytes
       ids 1ec6e1ff50273e64c93aa3113743b24660dbef48abfb69dd1d43a28b60d68706
       text 7d7754436326bf2bfb1b90e76ea55382d33391535524220ca34808627be7689e
    d  5 ids  "The capital of France is"                    txt 24 bytes
       ids 4ea817650cb7ca876196e3c286286ac30f2bc41c61b859b70f914ac1cf77482e
       text bbaff4d2ecd5892d4a442b0f53131641bf6e6f284761dd20fc0664bc97145762
    e  93 ids  a, b and c in order (no text: the ids are the three files' lines in a row, `cat a.ids b.ids c.ids`)
       ids fbcdb48d605f1321937f6ea41553fad89337b2819c9cec67833bb037d37098c8
       the fixture's selector keeps top_k 64 cells and its window is 64, which a, b, c and d (at most 32 ids, 8 pools of 4) never
       exceed. e has 93 ids = 23 pools of 4 and one id in a partial group, so it alone reaches three clauses: the selection (23
       pools against the 15 plus the open group it picks), the window layers' truncation (the last row sees 64 of its 93 positions)
       and the pooled tail (the one-id open group). `crates/tokenizer/tests/hy4.rs` holds it as the three in a row.
